{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For</b>: It is known that there are seven spheres for the luminaries and five for the wandering stars, and the eighth sphere for the great host, and the ninth for the sphere of the zodiac signs, which moves from east to west, and the tenth is the throne of glory. Therefore he wrote: \"the work of Your fingers,\" for they are ten. And he mentioned the moon and the stars and did not mention the sun, because the eye has no power to see them by day because of the light of the sun." "And some say: that the meaning of \"Your majesty\" — concerns the sun, for it is the great creation, and behold, it is not seen by day, but only one, and at night a very great host is seen."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The word מאורות (luminaries) is phonetically and conceptually identical to מעונות (spheres/dwellings) in medieval Hebrew manuscripts; I read it as מאורות in the first clause (\"for the luminaries\") and מעונות in the second (\"for the wandering stars\"), yielding parallel constructions."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:39.111007148Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}